// Sprint 4 ticket 02 — Vault policy for the kubinate-api workload.
//
// Scope:
//
// 1. Transit-engine encrypt/decrypt on `<key_prefix>/*` keys. The
//    application creates one key per organization
//    (`<key_prefix>/<organization_id>`) lazily during the first
//    put; this glob covers every present and future tenant.
// 2. The `keys/<name>` create endpoint, also globbed under the
//    same prefix, so the lazy ensure_key path doesn't require
//    operator pre-provisioning.
//
// CRITICAL: `vault_kubinate_key_prefix` (default `kubinate`) MUST
// match the `KUBINATE__VAULT_KEY_PREFIX` env var on the API binary,
// which defaults to `kubinate` in `crates/api/src/main.rs`. If the
// two diverge, the API gets 403 on every encrypt / decrypt call
// because the AppRole's policy doesn't cover the path the API is
// hitting. **Do not collapse this with `vault_kubinate_role_name`**
// — they're independent on purpose; the role name belongs to the
// AppRole binding, the prefix belongs to the key namespace.
//
// Notably absent:
// - No `read` capability on transit keys. The application doesn't
//   need to introspect key metadata; the encrypt/decrypt
//   permissions are enough.
// - No access outside the prefix's namespace. A compromised AppRole
//   token cannot reach any secret outside the application's own
//   scope.

path "transit/encrypt/{{ vault_kubinate_key_prefix }}/*" {
  capabilities = ["update"]
}

path "transit/decrypt/{{ vault_kubinate_key_prefix }}/*" {
  capabilities = ["update"]
}

path "transit/keys/{{ vault_kubinate_key_prefix }}/*" {
  capabilities = ["create", "update"]
}
